# SSSF environment. Copy to .env at the target repo root and fill in.
#
# THE DEFAULT ROSTER NEEDS NOTHING HERE.
# It runs `coding_agent: claude_code`, which drives headless `claude -p` on the
# Claude Code session you are already logged into. No key, no config — just
# `claude --version` and a working `claude -p 'hi'`.
#
# DO NOT SET ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
# It would not take effect anyway: agent_cc strips ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS,
# CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK and CLAUDE_CODE_USE_VERTEX from every agent it spawns.
# That is deliberate. The justfile does `set dotenv-load` and operator_env()
# copies the whole environment through, so one stray key in this file would
# otherwise move every agent from your subscription onto per-token API billing —
# identical output, identical trace, a different invoice. If you genuinely want
# API billing, edit agent_cc.API_AUTH_VARS and mean it.
#
# KEYS BELOW ARE ONLY FOR AGENTS YOU PUT ON `coding_agent: pi`.
# Every `model:` in adws/adw_sssf_config/sssf.config.yaml is written as
# provider/model-id. The provider half decides which key must be set, and which
# key pi reads for that provider comes from ~/.pi/agent/models.json. Example:
#   google/gemini-3.6-flash                      served via openrouter -> OPENROUTER_API_KEY
#   fireworks/accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3  fireworks             -> FIREWORKS_API_KEY
#   openai/gpt-5.6-terra                         openai                -> OPENAI_API_KEY
#
# Point every pi agent at one provider and you only need that provider's key.
#
# Nothing validates this for you. `agents.validate()` checks that a model is
# written as provider/id and that a pi model is in pi's catalog — not that the
# provider is reachable or that its key is set, so a missing key shows up when
# that agent runs, not at startup.

# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# FIREWORKS_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides
# CLAUDE_PATH=claude               # claude binary if not on PATH
# PI_PATH=pi                       # pi binary if not on PATH
# PI_MODELS_PATH=~/.pi/agent/models.json
# ENGINEER_NAME=                   # engineer lane label, defaults to git user.name
